// Title: Uncommon Child Process Of BgInfo.EXE
// Sigma ID: aaf46cdc-934e-4284-b329-34aa701e3771
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), Beyu Denis, oscd.community
// Date: 2019-10-26 | Modified: 2023-08-16
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1059.005, T1218, T1202
// Description: Detects uncommon child processes of "BgInfo.exe" which could be a sign of potential abuse of the
//   binary to proxy execution via external VBScript
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/Bginfo/
//   - https://oddvar.moe/2017/05/18/bypassing-application-whitelisting-with-bginfo/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_bginfo_uncommon_child_process.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\bginfo.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\bginfo64.exe"
